        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add plan-first Claw status and remove",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- add experimental `claws status [claw-or-agent]` with canonical agent, workspace-file, and package state\n- bind `claws remove` consent to a dry-run `planIntegrity` digest and revalidate the complete plan before mutation\n- reuse canonical agent deletion plus existing plugin and skill uninstall lifecycles\n- remove only a final, unchanged, Claw-origin package that has not been adopted by a direct install\n- retain independently owned, shared, pending, failed, modified, missing, or ambiguous artifacts and report why\n\n## Scope\n\nThis is the status/remove slice for the grouped one-Claw/one-agent contract. Package names resolve an install only when unambiguous; final agent ids always work and disambiguate repeated adds.\n\nRemove is a two-step operation. The dry-run records the expected agent identity, managed-file digests, package ownership and canonical state, and root install state in `planIntegrity`. Mutation requires `--yes --plan-integrity <digest>`, rebuilds the plan, and fails closed if any consent-bearing input changed. Agent drift and unsafe workspace paths block the plan. Missing files are already removed, locally modified files are retained, and unchanged files are moved to nonce staging paths before final validation and deletion.\n\nPackage ownership is order-independent. Every Claw reference records whether the package originated from a Claw or existed independently. A later direct plugin or skill install adopts matching references as independently owned. Canonical install timestamps provide a conservative fallback if adoption state cannot be recorded. A final unchanged Claw-origin package is removed only after ownership is re-read immediately before execution, and deletion delegates to the existing plugin or skill uninstall lifecycle. Shared, adopted, drifted, incomplete, or uncertain packages are retained.\n\nIf package or file cleanup fails after the agent config commit, the root ledger remains partial and subordinate references stay available for status/doctor recovery. All commands remain gated by `OPENCLAW_EXPERIMENTAL_CLAWS=1`, and JSON contracts remain experimental.\n\n## Stack\n\n- RFC: https://github.com/openclaw/rfcs/pull/27\n- Depends on: #102228 package installation, ownership, and references\n- This PR: lifecycle visibility and consent-bound, ownership-aware cleanup\n- Next: #102306 portable export from the same provenance ledger\n\n## Validation\n\n- `node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p test/tsconfig/tsconfig.test.src.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/test-src.tsbuildinfo`\n- Oxlint: 0 warnings, 0 errors across all 17 touched files\n- Oxfmt check: all 17 touched files correctly formatted\n- 30 focused status/remove/package-adoption tests\n- 14 Claws CLI tests\n- 158 canonical plugin install tests\n- 74 canonical skill install tests\n- 7 full lifecycle E2E tests\n- `git diff --check`\n- Codex review: no accepted/actionable findings\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n`src/claws/lifecycle.e2e.test.ts` invokes the real `src/entry.ts` CLI in an isolated state directory and passes the complete add -> status -> remove dry-run -> digest-bound consented remove flow. The final result is `openclaw.clawRemoveResult.v1` with `status: \"complete\"`; canonical agent config is removed and the managed workspace file is deleted.\n",
